 "approach": "Apply ref-002's hypothesis-induced divergence measure to quantify distributional shifts between clean and poisoned data. Train surrogate models (same architecture as the target model) on clean (source) and poisoned (target) datasets. Compute divergence scores using ref-002's formula: $D(P, Q) = \frac{1}{n} \text{sup}_{h \neq h'} |P(h(x) = y) - Q(h(x) = y)|$. High divergence scores indicate backdoor presence. The approach differs from ref-001 by replacing activation clustering with this divergence metric and from ref-009 by using model predictions rather than perturbation-induced entropy.",
